# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (RCA 2026-07-28, .agent/reports/202607/20260725_30_…):
# the VSN1 layout-deploy tool compiles Lua templates into device action
# strings, and its comment stripper split on '\n'. This repo has
# core.autocrlf=true and had NO .gitattributes, so every checkout materialized
# the templates as CRLF — every line then ended in '\r', the comment regex
# could never match, not one comment was stripped, and the encoder INIT action
# string went 904 → 5960 chars against a 909-char device limit. Every deploy
# failed, on every boot and every effect change.
#
# The stripper now splits on /\r?\n/ (lua_action_string.cjs), so CRLF is
# harmless on its own. This file kills the drift class at the source: Lua is
# consumed byte-for-byte by a device compiler and must stay LF in the working
# tree, on every platform.
#
# NOTE: adding an attribute does NOT rewrite an ALREADY-CHECKED-OUT tree. Run
#   git add --renormalize .
# once (see the _31 report) to bring existing working copies into line.
*.lua text eol=lf
